WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.235 --> 00:00:25.500
Jonathan hurried to his parents. "You told me you'd back me up if I needed you. I need you. Thanks!" he added, rushing back to his team.

2
00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:31.736
Max spoke before Coach Wattenbarger could start talking. "I feel well enough to play the second half of the game.

3
00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:35.673
But my teammates should get the ball more. It's only fair."

4
00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:40.831
Coach Wattenbarger crossed his arms. "My job is to help this team win."

5
00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:45.673
Jonathan raised his hand. "Max's suggestion will help us win, Coach.

6
00:00:45.674 --> 00:00:48.813
Giving him the ball all the time could make him sick again.

7
00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:51.173
We don't want to lose the best player in the league."

8
00:00:51.174 --> 00:00:54.230
The coach just stared at Jonathan.

9
00:00:54.231 --> 00:01:01.071
Then Mrs. Cho, who had come over to stand behind Jonathan, spoke up. "My son deserves more opportunities with the ball."

10
00:01:01.072 --> 00:01:06.306
"My son too," Carlos' mother added. "I need to look out for my baby boy!"

11
00:01:06.307 --> 00:01:08.568
A few more parents chimed in.

12
00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:16.178
Coach Wattenbarger stood there, listening. His face had reddened, as if he were upset or embarrassed or both.

13
00:01:16.179 --> 00:01:18.882
"Please, Dad," Max said.

14
00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:25.047
"I don't want to be a ball hog. Can't we play with two forwards and pass to whichever player is open?"

15
00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:27.720
"Perfect idea!" Mrs. Cho said.

16
00:01:27.721 --> 00:01:30.228
Finally, Coach Wattenbarger sighed.

17
00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:36.442
"All right. We'll try it your way, Max. I don't want to overwork you or set the team against you.

18
00:01:36.443 --> 00:01:39.950
And maybe it's not too late to turn this game around."

19
00:01:39.951 --> 00:01:45.107
Jonathan exchanged smiles with Max and Carlos. Then everyone thanked the coach.

20
00:01:45.108 --> 00:01:48.428
"You won't be sorry, Coach!" Jonathan promised.

21
00:01:48.429 --> 00:01:53.609
The teams returned to the field for the second half of the game.

22
00:01:53.610 --> 00:02:04.184
Carlos passed the ball to Jonathan. Before Jonathan could do anything with the ball, the huge Spitting Cobra ran in front of him.

23
00:02:04.185 --> 00:02:12.169
Max was closely guarded by another Cobra, so Jonathan passed the ball back to Carlos.

24
00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.677
One of the Cobras stole the ball and kicked it to his teammate.

25
00:02:15.678 --> 00:02:21.567
The Cobras passed the ball up the field a few yards at a time. The Wattenbargers couldn't stop them.

26
00:02:21.568 --> 00:02:28.099
A Cobra forward took a shot.

27
00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:32.150
The ball rocketed through the air, above the reach of the Wattenbarger goalie.

28
00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:35.981
As the ball soared, Jonathan's heart sank.

29
00:02:35.982 --> 00:02:43.123
But the ball hit the metal goal post and bounced out of bounds. Phew!

30
00:02:43.124 --> 00:02:53.299
The Wattenbarger goalie kicked the ball high and hard. A Wattenbarger midfielder jumped up and headed it toward an open part of the field.

31
00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.433
Max wasn't close to the ball, but he ran as if he had wings on his feet.

32
00:02:57.434 --> 00:03:05.869
He got to the ball while it was still in the air, heading it down so that it landed in front of him.

33
00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:11.296
Then he took a very long shot, surprising everyone—including the Cobras' goalie.

34
00:03:11.297 --> 00:03:20.114
The ball sailed into the goal. Max had tied the score, 1–1.

35
00:03:20.115 --> 00:03:24.293
"Awesome!" Jonathan shouted as cheers broke out around him.

36
00:03:24.294 --> 00:03:30.601
Jonathan and Max jogged together to the center circle for the next kickoff.

37
00:03:30.602 --> 00:03:37.172
"Max, I know two things about you," Jonathan said. "One, you were never really sick today.

38
00:03:37.173 --> 00:03:40.900
And two, you're definitely the best player in the league."

39
00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:44.917
Max grinned. "And the best-looking player in the league."

40
00:03:44.918 --> 00:03:48.430
Jonathan grinned back. "Not even close."

41
00:03:48.431 --> 00:03:57.265
After the kickoff a Cobra forward dribbled the ball up the field, but Carlos ran in front of him and forced him out of bounds.

42
00:03:57.266 --> 00:04:04.018
Carlos took the throw-in, landing the ball directly in front of Jonathan's foot.

43
00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:08.417
Jonathan dribbled the ball forward only a few yards before a Cobra midfielder stole it.

44
00:04:08.418 --> 00:04:10.167
Jonathan groaned.

45
00:04:10.168 --> 00:04:17.825
If Carlos had thrown the ball to Max instead, Max probably could have used his superior speed and ball control to make another goal.

46
00:04:17.826 --> 00:04:26.477
The Cobra midfielder passed the ball to a forward, who kicked it into the goal. Jonathan groaned again.

47
00:04:26.478 --> 00:04:29.697
The Cobras were back in the lead, 2–1.

48
00:04:29.698 --> 00:04:38.316
As the Cobras and their coach and fans cheered, Jonathan trudged back to the center circle.

49
00:04:38.317 --> 00:04:40.348
He hated disappointing his team.

50
00:04:40.349 --> 00:04:46.967
In a way, it had been easier when Max was hogging the ball, because he'd also gotten most of the blame when things went wrong.

51
00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:58.948
At the kickoff Jonathan passed the ball to Max. Max dribbled it far up the field, dodging the Cobras with his impressive footwork.

52
00:04:58.949 --> 00:05:06.519
Finally, he kicked the ball to Jonathan, who took a shot.

53
00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:09.530
The goalie caught the ball.

54
00:05:09.531 --> 00:05:12.853
Coach Wattenbarger yelled, "Oh, no!"

55
00:05:12.854 --> 00:05:16.171
Jonathan yelled much worse things to himself.

56
00:05:16.172 --> 00:05:21.106
Both teams played hard, getting the ball from one end of the field to the other and back again.

57
00:05:21.107 --> 00:05:28.948
With only a few minutes left in the game, the Wattenbarger right midfielder kicked the ball to Jonathan.

58
00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:35.321
A moment later two Spitting Cobra defenders ran in front of him. There was no way Jonathan could get around them.

59
00:05:35.322 --> 00:05:37.220
Or maybe there was.

60
00:05:37.221 --> 00:05:40.254
Jonathan remembered the double fake that Max had taught him.

61
00:05:40.255 --> 00:05:44.085
He lifted his left foot and quickly took a step to the left.

62
00:05:44.086 --> 00:05:53.889
In anticipation, the two Cobras shifted to the left. Jonathan suddenly sped to the right, escaping the Cobra defenders.

63
00:05:53.890 --> 00:06:00.148
He kicked the ball into the goal, tying the score.

64
00:06:00.149 --> 00:06:04.477
Jonathan's teammates cheered.

65
00:06:04.478 --> 00:06:10.556
Coach Wattenbarger shouted, "Nice job, Cho! You looked almost as good as Max!"

66
00:06:10.557 --> 00:06:15.370
Mrs. Cho yelled, "Yay, Johnnyb—I mean, Jonathan!"

67
00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:19.303
Best of all, Marissa yelled, "All right, Jonathan!"

68
00:06:19.304 --> 00:06:28.869
At the next kickoff, the Cobras took the ball close to the goal by passing it from one player to the next, showing awesome teamwork.

69
00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:37.292
But the Wattenbargers also had awesome teamwork. A Wattenbarger defender intercepted the ball and kicked it away.

70
00:06:37.293 --> 00:06:41.364
Another Wattenbarger defender saved it before it could go out of bounds.

71
00:06:41.365 --> 00:06:48.516
He kicked it to Carlos, who dribbled the ball up the field and passed it to Jonathan.

72
00:06:48.517 --> 00:06:53.347
Jonathan was pretty far from the goal but thought he might be able to kick the ball in.

73
00:06:53.348 --> 00:06:58.272
It would be awesome to make the game-winning goal, though the odds of doing that were small.

74
00:06:58.273 --> 00:07:03.771
He looked around. Max was open, but he stood as far from the goal as Jonathan did.

75
00:07:03.772 --> 00:07:11.438
Jonathan loved making goals. But he also loved making smart plays, especially when the score was tied, and the game was almost over.

76
00:07:11.439 --> 00:07:17.008
So he quickly kicked the ball to the best player in the league.

77
00:07:17.009 --> 00:07:19.571
Max took a fast shot at the goal.

78
00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:29.322
The goalie dived for the ball, but it soared over his head. The Wattenbargers had their third goal!

79
00:07:29.323 --> 00:07:33.747
The referee blew his whistle, announcing the end of the game.

80
00:07:33.748 --> 00:07:37.107
A 3–2 win: Team Wattenbarger!

81
00:07:37.108 --> 00:07:40.842
Jonathan cheered loudly.

82
00:07:40.843 --> 00:07:45.896
"Today we played like a team," he thought, "and that's what matters most."

83
00:07:45.897 --> 00:07:54.320
But winning the game sure felt great too.
